    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode. Changes:\n\n**`OwnerLocality.java`** \u2014 Added a `derive(String city, String postcode)` overload that:\n1. First maps the postcode to a region by range (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099).\n2. Falls back to the existing city-to-region table only when the postcode is `null`, malformed, or in no known range.\n\nThe original single-arg `derive(String city)` is retained unchanged.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 The `locality` mapping expression now passes the postcode: `OwnerLocality.derive(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode())`.\n\nThe controller's `validatePostcode` deliberately keeps calling the city-only `derive(city)` \u2014 postcode validity must still be checked against the *city's* region, not derived circularly from the postcode itself.\n\nBoth tests pass: `coreRegionFromPostcodeRange` (Sydney/2000 \u2192 NSW) and `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity` (unknown city + 3000 \u2192 VIC, proving postcode precedence). `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
