    "probe_text": "Confirmed. Here is the complete, ordered sequence of every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`.\n\nThe endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:176`), which implements the generated `OwnersApi` interface (class-level `@RequestMapping(\"/api\")` + interface `POST /owners`).\n\n## A. Before the controller body runs (framework-level)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role or the request is denied (`AccessDeniedException`).\n2. **Bean Validation of the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`** \u2014 checked *before* any controller code, on the raw (un-normalized) body. Failure \u2192 HTTP 400 via `handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$\")`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$\")`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)` (optional/nullable)\n   - `postcode`, `registrationDate`, `sharesHousehold`: no declarative constraints\n\n## B. Controller body \u2014 validations & normalizations, in exact order\n\nThese are imperative private methods (no custom `ConstraintValidator` classes exist). Each runs in the order below:\n\n3. `normalizeAddress` \u2014 trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. (Mutates the DTO *after* Bean Validation already ran.)\n4. `validateRequiredFields` \u2014 trims and rejects blank/whitespace-only `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`; offending fields \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n5. `normalizeTelephone` \u2014 converts to E.164: strips non-digits, assumes `+61` if no country code, drops a leading `0`, requires 8\u201315 digits, enforces per-country national length (`+1`\u219210, `+61`\u21929); invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException([\"telephone\"])` (400).\n6. `normalizeEmail` \u2014 if present, must match the email pattern, then lower-cased; invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException([\"email\"])` (400).\n7. `validatePostcode` \u2014 if present, must be 4 digits and within the region range derived from `city` (`OwnerLocality.derive`); invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException([\"postcode\"])` (400).\n8. `rejectDuplicateIdentity(..., resolveHouseholdId(...))` \u2014 reads all owners; rejects if identity key `telephone|email|householdId` already exists \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (409).\n9. `rejectCityAtCapacity` \u2014 case-insensitive count of owners in the city; if \u2265 50 \u2192 `OwnerCityAtCapacityException` (409).\n10. `resolveRegistrationDate` \u2014 defaults to `LocalDate.now()` if absent, then rolls a weekend date forward to Monday; **writes the value back into the DTO**.\n11. `rejectDailyLimitReached(registrationDate)` \u2014 count of owners with the same registration date; if \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitReachedException` (429).\n\n## C. Mapping & derived-value side-effects (mutating the new Owner), in order\n\n12. `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` \u2014 MapStruct maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` (ignores id, pets, customerCode).\n13. `assignCustomerCode` \u2014 sets `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` customer code.\n14. `assignMembershipNumber` \u2014 sets membership number.\n15. `assignNamesakeCount` \u2014 counts existing owners with the same name.\n16. `assignMembershipLevel` \u2014 sets membership level.\n17. `assignBulkSignupWarning` \u2014 sets warning flag (threshold 80).\n18. `assignHousehold` \u2014 resolves/creates a `householdId` (SHA-256 of `lastName|address`); **may call `saveOwner` on pre-existing owners** to back-fill a shared household id (side-effect on *other* rows).\n19. `assignHouseholdMembership` \u2014 sets household member count.\n\n## D. Persistence & final side-effects\n\n20. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 `@Transactional`; `em.persist` (DB assigns the id). Note `addOwner` itself is **not** transactional, so each read/save is its own transaction.\n21. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"owner created id=... customerCode=... registrationDate=... membershipLevel=...\")` (SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`).\n22. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` \u2014 builds response DTO (derives `displayName`, `initials`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey` \u2014 response-only).\n23. Sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and returns **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notable absences\n- **No** JPA entity lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/`@EntityListeners`) on `Owner`, `Person`, or `BaseEntity`.\n- **No** application events published, and **no** emails sent.\n- The `Owner` entity carries its own `@NotEmpty` / `@Pattern(\"^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` constraints, but these only fire if the entity is validated on flush \u2014 they are not explicitly triggered in this path.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: because `normalizeAddress` (step 3) runs *after* Bean Validation (step 2), the `@Size`/`@Pattern` constraints on `address` are checked against the raw input, not the normalized value."
  },
